Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 21:43:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07161/11362] [outer-loop] exp5713: Qwen3.6-27B Q4+Q8KV+MTP
 hits a hard OOM, not a quality result (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5599-4)

Operator asked to try Qwen3.6-27B 4bit quant one last time with Q8
KV-cache. Checked the record first: exp5599 already ran this exact
config cleanly at n=3 (0/3 plan rate, mean 401s) -- re-running verbatim
would be a doomed rerun. Surfaced this via AskUserQuestion; operator
chose to isolate the one untested variable: mtp=False was set with no
recorded rationale despite the model being named *-MTP-GGUF.

Real finding: MTP structurally cannot run for this model on this
hardware. Self-speculative MTP loads the same GGUF file TWICE (target
+ draft, two separate CUDA buffers). Target loads fine (~15.9GiB);
draft alloc fails with a hard cudaMalloc OOM trying to reserve another
~15.6GiB on top -- total ~32.6GB exceeds the single RTX 3090's 24GB.
Almost certainly the undocumented reason exp5599 set mtp=False in the
first place.

The background n=3 run initially stalled polling a crashed (<defunct>)
llama-server for up to 20min/repeat with DEVNULL-redirected output
hiding the crash reason. Killed and diagnosed manually instead, then
added a real precondition check (2x on-disk file size vs free VRAM,
not a magic number) so the experiment now blocks in <1s with the
concrete numbers, with the manual diagnostic's crash log embedded
verbatim in the artifact as evidence.

Sibling fix, same incident: adversarial_verify.py's
_is_precondition_check_only_blocked only recognized a bare "blocked_"
prefix, missing the "complete: blocked_<resource>" form CLAUDE.md's
own Verdict Terminal-Prefix Discipline mandates -- false-flagged this
experiment's correctly-formed blocked artifact DURATION_TOO_SHORT.
exp5705/exp5709's blocked branches use the identical pattern and would
have hit the same false positive. Fixed via
_strip_verdict_terminal_prefix; full adversarial_verify suite (309
tests) still green.

Answers the operator's original question: Q4_K_M+Q8-KV-cache
Qwen3.6-27B has now been tried as thoroughly as this hardware allows
(MTP off: 0/3 clean; MTP on: structurally impossible). Neither beats
the frozen 9B. Frozen live-submission generator remains unchanged.
